{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1792310627,"nonce":"LLpOT96nPJwgErZvblkB/kBgPGQ=","title":"Rayzor Bug Fix History (Pre-2026-02-13)","message":"Older bug fixes moved here from MEMORY.md to keep the main file under 200 lines.\n\n**Problem**: SIMD4f methods intermittently returned 0 or crashed. Chained calls like `a.sqrt().sum()` failed.\n**Root Causes**: FALLBACK2 excluded SIMD (brute-force picked Tensor methods), chained call receiver typed as Dynamic.\n**Fix**: SIMD4f direct lookup when `convert_type().is_vector()`, register type fallback for Dynamic receivers, MIR wrapper registration.\n\n**Problem**: `@:op(A + B)` with `(rhs : Int)` returned wrong values. `ExprKind::TypeCheck` lowered as boolean instead of Cast.\n**Fix**: Changed to `TypedExpressionKind::Cast`, added Cast/FieldAccess handlers to `inline_expression_deep`.\n\n**Problem**: `var d:Dynamic = {x: 1, y: 2}; trace(d.x);` crashed. Dynamic anon objects couldn't be read/written.\n**Fix**: `dynamic_reflect_field_read()` helper + `field_exists_in_any_class()` discriminator. Unbox first via `haxe_unbox_reference_ptr`.\n\n**Problem**: `test_generics.hx` crashed after SRA field-0 fix enabled more candidates. `next_reg_id` was stale.\n**Fix**: Recompute `next_reg_id` at start of `apply_sra`.\n\n**Problem**: `replace_uses()` missing for all 9 vector instructions. Inliner never remapped their operands.\n**Fix**: Added explicit match arms for all vector and Move/Clone instructions.\n\n**Problem**: `var a:SIMD4f = [1.0, ...]` failed. SIMD4f not in `file.abstracts`, `@:from` rules never populated.\n**Fix**: Added `try_stdlib_from_cast()` fallback for direct stdlib mapping lookup.\n\n**Problem**: `(x:Int) -\u003e x * 2` applied to 21 returns 0. Four bugs in parser, AST lowering, and lambda params.\n**Fix**: `ArrowParam` struct, `create_variable_with_type`, register in `function.locals`, unwrap single-expr blocks.\n\n**Problem**: Two classes in same file -\u003e crash. Pre-computed SRA locations stale after first modification.\n**Fix**: Process ONE SRA candidate per pass, re-analyze after each.\n\n**Problem**: `Box\u003cBox\u003cInt\u003e\u003e` chained `.get().get()` crashed. TypeParameter fell through to stdlib `Arc.get()`.\n**Fix**: Extended `receiver_is_user_class` for TypeParameter/GenericInstance.\n\n**Problem**: `Reflect.hasField(p, \"x\")` returned false. Shapes not registered at runtime.\n**Fix**: Added `rayzor_ensure_shape()` emitted before each `rayzor_anon_new`.\n\n**Problem**: stdlib function IDs collided with user functions.\n**Fix**: Update `next_function_id` after each stdlib function insert.\n\n**Problem**: `Body.Sun()` static method calls in nbody crashed with \"Cast source not found\" (Cranelift) / \"LLVM verification failed\" (LLVM).\n**Root Cause**: Static method call sites use different SymbolIds than the method definitions. E.g., `Body.Sun()` call uses SymbolId(2086) but the `Sun` method is registered with SymbolId(2189). The call resolution only searched `function_map` by symbol ID, then `external_function_map` by qualified name. When both failed, it created a forward-reference stub function with an unreachable entry block. The inlining pass then copied this stub into callers.\n**Fix**: In `hir_to_mir.rs` call resolution (~line 7864), also search `function_map` (local functions) by qualified name before falling through to external_function_map.\n\n**Problem**: Field assignments in class constructors and methods (like `i = inI` where `i` is a field) were not being converted to proper field access expressions (`this.i = inI`).\n**Root Cause**: Two issues:\n1. In AST lowering, when an identifier was resolved to a field symbol, it still created `Variable` instead of `FieldAccess` with implicit `this`.\n2. In HIR-MIR lowering, the implicit `this` variable had a different SymbolId than the synthetic `SymbolId::from_raw(0)` used for `this` in constructors.\n**Fix**: AST lowering creates FieldAccess with implicit `this` for field symbols. HIR-MIR redirects non-synthetic `this` SymbolId to `SymbolId::from_raw(0)`.\n\n**Problem**: The run command compiled code but never executed main function.\n**Fix**: Added `backend.execute_function(main_func_id, vec![])` call in `run_file()` (src/main.rs:666). Also needed `TieredBackend::with_symbols()` to pass runtime symbols.\n\n**Problem**: `static inline var MaxRad = 1 \u003c\u003c 16;` -\u003e MaxRad was null at runtime\n**Root Cause**: `try_evaluate_const_expr()` only handled Add/Sub/Mul/Div but not bit shift operators\n**Fix**: Added Shl, Shr, BitAnd, BitOr, BitXor, Mod operators to constant evaluation\n\n**Problem**: `static inline var X = 1000; trace(4/X);` -\u003e 0 (wrong)\n**Root Cause**: Field type defaulted to `dynamic_type()` instead of inferring from initializer\n**Fix**: In `ast_lowering.rs`, lower initializer first and use `init_expr.expr_type` when no type hint present\n\n**Problem**: `arr[2] = 999;` stored wrong value (3 instead of 999)\n**Root Cause**: `haxe_box_int_ptr()` returns `DynamicValue*` (type_id=3 for Int). Old code used it for array set, copying type_id instead of value.\n**Fix**: Created typed `haxe_array_set_i64()` and `haxe_array_set_f64()` that take values directly.\n**IMPORTANT**: Do NOT change `haxe_box_int_ptr` to return raw value - it's used for Dynamic type boxing. Array set must use separate typed functions.\n\n**Problem**: `arr[10] = 42;` on empty array -\u003e SIGSEGV\n**Fix**: `haxe_array_set_i64/f64/null` auto-expand array capacity and length when index \u003e= current length\n\n**Problem**: `arr[10] = null;` crashed\n**Fix**: MIR lowering passes null (0) via `haxe_array_set_i64`. Also added `haxe_array_set_null` for explicit null stores.\n\n**Problem**: nbody crashed with `malloc: Incorrect checksum for freed object` -- Body objects freed prematurely.\n**Root Cause**: `build_derived_set()` in `insert_free.rs` tracked `Cast`, `GEP`, `Copy` but NOT `BitCast`. Body pointers were bitcast to i64 before array push, so escape wasn't detected.\n**Fix**: Added `IrInstruction::BitCast` to the match arm alongside `Cast` in `build_derived_set()`.\n\n**Problem**: `icmp slt i32 %phi_50, i64 %call8` -- LLVM requires same-type operands.\n**Fix**: Added `coerce_ints` helper in `llvm_jit_backend.rs` that sign-extends the narrower operand.\n\n**Problem**: After inlining, `const 0i32` stored directly to f64 struct fields (NaN corruption).\n**Root Cause**: Haxe allows `new Body(0, 0, 0, ...)` where 0 is Int but params are Float. MIR didn't insert casts.\n**Fix**: In `builder.rs` `build_call_direct`, check argument vs parameter types and insert Cast for int\u003c-\u003efloat mismatches.\n\n**Problem**: SRA + CopyProp exposes `fmul` results directly to `fadd`, triggering cross-block FMA fusion that changes FP rounding (checksum 112798515 -\u003e 112798531)\n**Root Cause**: SRA replaces store/load through memory with direct register use. CopyProp removes intermediate copies. This exposes cross-block fmul-\u003efadd which `try_extract_fmul` sees as fma opportunity.\n**Fix**: In `try_extract_fmul` (instruction_lowering.rs), only fuse when fmul is in the **same Cranelift block** as the fadd/fsub.\n**Key insight**: FMA on magnitude check (same block) is harmless. FMA on iteration step (cross-block after SRA) changes actual z values.\n\n---\nArchived from Claude memory `bugs_history` on 2026-10-18. A record of past work; open items in it may have their own issues.","files":null}]}